ucer/test_reducer_cache.py:180) asserts the `.cache.json` mtime changes between the warm write and the post-deletion rewrite, using float `st_mtime`.\n- In an ubuntu:26.04 container on a colima VM (Linux 6.8.0-117-generic, aarch64, overlayfs /tmp), 2026-11-09 PST, the test failed 16 of 30 runs with no sandbox and 18 of 30 under bwrap, each failure reading `assert 1794262869.4604867 != 1794262869.4604867`.\n- It passes on GitHub's hosted runners (all pytest cells and run 42702801672's jobs passed).\n- It is in the `reducer-processors` mutation shard, so a failure there fails that shard's clean baseline (`baseline-test: head/reducer-processors`), as seen when reproducing `unwasteful-increased-colt` locally.\n\n## Hypotheses (unproven)\nThe two writes land within one kernel timestamp tick on hosts whose file timestamps are coarse (jiffy granularity), so the rewrite gets an identical mtime; or the second `reduce_ticket` call does not rewrite the cache on those hosts. Not yet distinguished.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] The root cause is identified with a deterministic reproduction, and the test asserts cache recomputation in a way that does not depend on timestamp granularity.","env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","file_impact":[],"file_impact_scope":"undeclared","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":[],"ticket_id":"d45f-229f-effe-4cf8","ticket_type":"bug","title":"test_cache_invalidated_on_file_deletion fails about half the time on a coarse-timestamp Linux host (equal mtime after rewrite)","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["4bcd0452-751d-4824-bf65-751db2eac90f","a7df9afc-b72f-44cf-bbc5-abfefeb2d114"]},"env_id":"","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1794263098127528002,"uuid":"f4e319f4-0457-4d55-83dc-8a9a513fb599"}